.TH IOWATCHD-LOG 1 "October 2026" "iowatchd 0.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iowatchd-log \- show the alerts logged by iowatchd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iowatchd-log
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shortcut to read the iowatchd log and the service state. The log file is the
\fBlog_file\fR of \fI/etc/iowatchd.conf\fR (or of \fB$IOWATCHD_CONFIG\fR),
\fI/var/log/iowatchd.log\fR by default. If file logging is disabled, the
systemd journal is read instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-lines\fR \fIN\fR
Show the last \fIN\fR lines (default 50). A bare \fIN\fR works too.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-follow\fR
Follow the log in real time.
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fIWHEN\fR
Only show entries since \fIWHEN\fR, in any format understood by
\fBdate\fR(1) \fB\-d\fR, e.g. "2026-10-17 08:00" or "1 hour ago".
Cannot be combined with \fB\-\-follow\fR.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Only show JSON entries (see \fBlog_format\fR); pretty-printed if \fBjq\fR(1)
is installed.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-status\fR
Show the service status (systemd, OpenRC or runit).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Do not page the \fB\-\-status\fR output.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IOWATCHD_LOG
Log file to read, overriding the configuration.
.TP
.B IOWATCHD_CONFIG
Configuration file to take \fBlog_file\fR from.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the log cannot be read, 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iowatchd (8),
.BR iowatchd.conf (5)
